Local extraction of the published virtual-fields method follows RECOLO, copyright2021 Sindre Nordmark Olufsen and Rene Kaufmann, MIT License preserved in LICENSE. Method: Kaufmann, Ganapathisubramani and Pierron(2019), DOI10.1007/s11340-019-00530-2; software: Olufsen et al.(2022), DOI10.21105/joss.03980.
Observation provenance: Experimental data for force reconstruction using impact hammer and deflectometry, DOI10.18710/TKS7SI, CC0. Complete280 camera frames were processed using the author's original example (first30 reference, remaining250 observations); derived measured deflection fields were losslessly stored in NPZ. No synthetic pressure or hidden target contributed to the public data. Independent hammer-force records remain maintainer validation measurements, not pixel pressure truth.


Acquisition correction: the original sparse slope integrator placed both coefficients of the first row-direction derivative at the same unknown, canceling that derivative row. A minimal private preprocessing correction changes its second column from the current row to the next row. A linear-ramp analytic test independently validates the correction. The actual bound deflection uses this corrected optical observation estimate; all subsequent original kinematics/Hermite/VFM mechanics functions are unchanged. The unmodified complete original pipeline is separately archived and compared in the notebook. No hammer-force or pressure target determined the correction.
